    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During those times when you are up early and feeling so energetic, have you noticed any unusual experiences, like hearing voices that others don't hear or feeling like you have special powers or abilities?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... I guess... I mean, I wouldn't call them special powers or anything like that. I just felt really, really capable, you know? Like I could handle anything that came my way. \n\nBut, um... well, since you asked... I guess during those times when I was all fired up and just sleeping a little bit, making all those big plans in the dark... I did start noticing some things. I probably shouldn't even mention it, because I know how it sounds, but... I'd hear my name being called, or like, short phrases, when there was nobody else in the house. I just tried to ignore it and focus on my plans, I really did. \n\nAnd, well, at work... I started getting this feeling. It's probably just me being overly cautious, because safety is so important, right? But I started feeling really sure that my supervisor was... well, setting traps for me. Like leaving things in my way on purpose to see if I'd mess up or get hurt. I know that probably sounds bad, and I didn't want to cause any trouble, I just wanted to do a good job. \n\nI'm sorry, I hope I'm not saying the wrong things. Is it normal to get a little confused or overly worried when you're that focused and energetic?",
